.  I will automatically detect it and set it up for you.  If you have a non-plug and play lighting system you will need to set it up manually using the LinuxMCE Admin Web Page.\r\n\r\nPlug and play lighting controllers: <%=12%>',1115,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1572,1,'Prepare ZWave Lighting',1116,549,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1573,1,'Cancel - I don\'t want to do this now',1117,549,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1574,1,'Do you have an alarm panel?',1118,344,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1575,1,'Found the alarm panel',1119,344,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1576,1,'Do you have a VOIP provider?',1120,344,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1577,1,'Configure Account',1121,349,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1578,1,'VOIP Username',1122,344,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1579,1,'VOIP Password',1123,349,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1580,1,'All done',1124,344,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1581,1,'Broadvoice',1125,347,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1582,1,'Free World Dialup',1126,347,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1583,1,'InPhonex',1127,347,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1584,1,'E-fon',1128,347,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1585,1,'Teliax',1129,347,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1586,1,'VOIP Number',1130,349,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1587,1,'Add\r\n+',1131,350,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1588,1,'Remove\r\n-',1132,350,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1589,1,'No, just make all the content public',1133,807,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1590,1,'Regarding your new storage device, can it be used automatically  for storing media, such as tv shows and music?',1134,351,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1591,1,'No, use it only when specifically told to',1135,351,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1592,1,'Use <-mkr_t_name_mixed->\'s directory structure so everyone can store both public and private media on this device?  This is recommended for a new, empty device that you will add media to using <-mkr_t_name_mixed->.  If the device already has content, or you will copy content to it from a PC, you will probably want to make all the content public for everyvone, or private for just the family member you select below.',1136,1036,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1593,1,'Enter your ZIP code or city name, then select \'Next\'.',1137,591,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1594,1,'I cannot find any location information for that Zip/Postal Code.  Please try another, perhaps that of a nearby city.',1138,353,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1600,1,'Please select one provider and then configure account',1144,355,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1601,1,'You choose Broadvoice,\r\nplease press configure account',1145,355,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1602,1,'Directly to TV',1146,355,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1603,1,'To a receiver',1147,355,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1604,1,'Neither, I have a special setup, like a scaler',1148,1041,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1605,1,'DSC',1149,357,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1606,1,'APEX',1150,357,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1607,1,'Installed AV Devices',1151,357,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1608,1,'Another AV Device',1152,357,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1609,1,'Alarm Panel Model',1153,357,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1610,1,'What port did you connect it to?',1154,357,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1611,1,'Looking for alarm panel...  Please wait',1155,357,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1612,1,'Panel not found',1156,357,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1613,1,'Which input on the TV is the receiver connected to?',1157,358,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1614,1,'Which input on the TV is this box connected to?',1158,358,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1615,1,'TV',1159,788,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1616,1,'ZWave Remote found.  Downloading data...',1160,627,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1617,1,'Error getting data',1161,364,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1618,1,'There are a total of <%=12%> lights in the house.\r\nThere are <%=13%> lights that have not yet been assigned to a room which we must identify.  Select Next to start.',1162,364,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1619,1,'It seems there are no lights in the controller.  Touch the \'back\' button to try again, or touch \'never mind\' to skip this.',1163,364,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1620,1,'Does this device have a video output that you connected into one of the other devices?  If yes, choose the device below.  Otherwise choose \'No\'.',1164,380,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1621,1,'Inputs',1165,366,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1622,1,'Does this device have an audio output that you connected into one of the other devices?  If yes, choose the device below.  Otherwise choose \'No\'.',1166,380,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1623,1,'Don\'t plug any new devices until the wizard finishes',1167,366,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1624,1,'After you press this button the system will spend some time generating the scenarios for all the devices that you have added.\r\nAfter that the main menu will show up.',1168,931,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1625,1,'<%=31%>',1169,366,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1626,1,'Which room is this system in?',1170,374,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1627,1,'Please enter your phone number for this phone <%=13%>',1171,374,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1628,1,'Cable/antenna input',1172,379,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1629,1,'External satellite/cable box',1173,379,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1630,1,'You have recently added or removed devices from the system.  I need to reload the router and all the devices in the house.  This takes about 15 seconds.  Shall I do this now?',1174,382,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1631,1,'Yes, do it now',1175,382,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1632,1,'No, do it later',1176,382,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1633,1,'You have recently changed scenarios, floorplans or other settings.  I need to regenerate the graphical screens so you can see the new buttons.  This takes anywhere from 2 to 20 minutes.',1177,382,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1634,1,'Yes, regenerate the screens for  this Orbiter',1178,382,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1635,1,'Yes, regenerate all Orbiters in my home',1179,382,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1636,1,'No, I\'ll do it later',1180,382,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1637,1,'No receiver',1181,632,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1638,1,'Control my receiver with infrared',1182,564,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1639,1,'Which security sensors can be viewed by this camera?  Select all that apply and then select \'OK\'',1183,392,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1640,1,'Display\r\nOn',1184,402,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1641,1,'Minimize LinuxMCE Orbiter',1185,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1642,1,'LinuxMCE has detected new software and has already downloaded it in background. You need to reboot LinuxMCE to install the new software.\r\n\r\nDo you want to reboot now?',1186,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1643,1,'Force Upgrade Now',1187,427,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1644,1,'Manufacturer isn’t on the list?',1188,427,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1645,1,'Welcome to the Monster THX demo room.\r\nPress a  button on the Monster Central remote for a demo:',1189,429,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1646,1,'IR Group',1190,431,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1647,1,'Which model do you have?',1191,431,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1648,1,'Learn Infrared codes',1192,527,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1649,1,'Connect directly to the TV?',1193,431,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1650,1,'Confirm the codes work',1194,431,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1651,1,'Please type in the model',1195,431,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1652,1,'List of all bookmarks',1196,437,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1653,1,'View bookmarks for this file',1197,437,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1654,1,'My Manufacturer isn\'t on the list',1198,447,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1655,1,'What Delay?',1199,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1656,1,'How to tune?',1200,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1657,1,'Do you have single or multiple video inputs?',1201,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1658,1,'Single Input',1202,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1659,1,'Multiple Inputs',1203,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1660,1,'Do you have DSP Modes with your TV?',1204,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1661,1,'No, my device has no DSP Modes',1205,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1662,1,'Yes, my device has DSP Modes',1206,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1663,1,'I have separate buttons for changing DSP Modes',1207,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1664,1,'I have a toggle button for DSP Modes',1208,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1665,1,'My model isn\'t on the list',1209,463,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1666,1,'<%=0%>',1210,471,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1667,1,'<%=0%>',1211,471,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1668,1,'<%=0%>',1212,471,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1669,1,'By default when it\'s time to tune to a station, channel or frequency, we assume this device wants you to punch in the number on the remote, and then hit \'enter\'. If that\'s correct, or if there are no number buttons on the remote for this device, click next. Otherwise\r\n\r\nIs there an Enter button on the remote you can hit after typing in numbers to make it tune right away?',1213,483,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1670,1,'Does the number of digits need to be padded to a fixed length in order to tune right away? Leave blank if \'no\'. Enter 3 for example if you always enter 3 digits, such as 012 to tune to \'12\' and 005 to tune to \'5\'.\r\nNumber of digits:',1214,483,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1671,1,'Toggle power or discrete?',1215,486,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1672,1,'Discrete power means there are separate on and off commands or buttons. So you can send the \'on\' command and even if the device is already on, it won\'t turn off. This makes it easy to control the device.\r\nToggle means there is only 1 button which toggles between on and off, called \'Toggle Power\'. You hit it once and it\'s on, hit it again and it\'s off. Whenever possible avoid devices with toggle because then it\'s possible to get out of sync, where the system sends a Toggle Power to turn it on, but in fact it really turned it off.',1216,486,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1673,1,' My device has discrete, separate on/off commands',1217,486,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1674,1,'My device only has a single toggle power button',1218,486,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1675,1,'Good news!  It seems we have some infrared codes to control [<%=31%>] by [<%=43%>].  We have [<%=33%>] set of infrared codes to try.  Below are buttons to send your [<%=31%>] an on and an off.  Please use the arrows to highlight each of the on/off buttons below  Press Enter to test the button and confirm it works.  Test each button several times in a row to be sure it does not also toggle the power.  In other words, if you test the on button the [<%=31%>] should come on.  If it does not, move over and press enter to check the box in the column \'does not work\'.  If it does work, try testing the on button again a few times.  The TV should always stay on, even when you test the on button several times in a row.  This is what we call \'discrete\' power, meaning we can send the on button several times to be sure the TV really does come on reliably every time.  If, however, when you send the on button again it actually turns the TV off, this is what we call a toggle code.  It will make it very difficult to control the TV since I can never be too sure if I am turning the TV on or off.  So if selecting the on button several times turns the TV off again, or if selecting the off button several times turns it on again, check the box \'toggle power\'.  If it works well without problems, then check the box \'this works\'.  Please do this for all the on off buttons below.',1219,895,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1676,1,'Confirm discrete power codes',1220,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1677,1,'Confirm toggle power codes',1221,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1678,1,'I  do have some infrared codes that may work with this [<%=31%>] by [<%=43%>].  Unfortunately these codes are what we call \'toggle\', that means the same code turns the device off and on, so I will never be completely sure whether I turned it on or off, and sometimes I may get it wrong. There is nothing that can be done about this.  If [<%=43%>] has only toggle buttons for their [<%=31%>\'s], they will be difficult to use with any universal remote control, or any home automation system.  However these days most manufacturers have decided to add discrete power codes, even if there is still not a button for it on the manufacturer\'s remote.  You may ask your dealer if he is able to get discrete codes for you.  If so, choose the button \'I have discrete codes\'.  Otherwise please go down the list and tests each of the \'power\' buttons.  If it works check the box \'this works\', if it does not, check the box \'doesn\'t work\'.',1222,509,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1679,1,'Most Sensitive',1223,502,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1680,1,'Middle Sensitivity',1224,502,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1681,1,'Least Sensitive',1225,502,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1682,1,'Filename',1226,505,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1683,1,'Choose the media type',1227,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1684,1,'Please select all the inputs this device has. If your device has an input that is not on the list, but there is a close match, choose that. It\'s not important that the wording be exactly the same',1228,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1685,1,'Here you will check off all the inputs, and for each indicate if it is a built-in source, or if the input is for connecting an external device to.\r\n\r\nFrom first column select an input then  go right to select the source and the connector type',1229,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1686,1,'Discrete or toggle inputs?',1230,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1687,1,'Discrete inputs means there are separate buttons or commands for all your TV inputs.\r\nToggle means that there is only a single button or command that toggles between all the inputs. Note it is especially difficult to control a device, like a TV, that has lots of inputs and only has a single toggle button. When hooking your equipment up you will likely want to use another device, like a receiver, that can handle the inputs discretely.',1231,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1688,1,'My device has discrete, separate commands for TV inputs',1232,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1689,1,'My device only has a single toggle inputs button ',1233,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1690,1,'Confirm discrete inputs codes',1234,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1691,1,'Good news!  It seems we have some infrared codes to set the inputs on [<%=31%>] by [<%=43%>].  We have [<%=33%>] set of infrared codes to try.  Below are buttons to send your [<%=31%>] the right input.  Be sure your TV is on and then go through each button below and test to confirm if it really does set your TV to the correct input.  If your TV does not go to that input when you select the button, check the box \'doesn\'t work\'.  If it does, try sending the command several times in a row to be sure it stays on the right input.  If it doesn\'t, that is if it starts changing inputs, check the box \'toggles input\'.  If it does go to an input and stay there, but the name of the inputs does not match the name of the button on-screen, choose the box \'works, but name doesn\'t match\'.  If it works in the name is correct, check the box \'this works\'.',1235,509,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1692,1,'I do have some infrared codes and may work with this [<%=31%>] by [<%=43%>].  Unfortunately these codes are what we call \'toggle\', meaning there is only one code to cycle through all the inputs, so I can never be too sure whether I really selected the right one are not, and sometimes I may get it wrong.  There is nothing they can be done about this.  If [<%=43%>] has only toggle codes for their [<%=31%>\'s], they will be difficult to use with any universal remote control, or any home automation system.  However these days most manufacturers have decided to add discrete input codes, even if there is still not a button for it on the manufactures remote.  You may ask your dealer if he is able to get discrete codes for you.  If so, choose the button I have discrete codes.  Otherwise go down the list and test each of the input buttons.  If it works check the box this works, if it does not check the box doesn\'t work.',1236,509,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1693,1,'Confirm toggle inputs codes',1237,507,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1694,1,' <%=33%>.\r\nShould LinuxMCE use it?',1238,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1695,1,'<%=0%>',1239,517,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1696,1,'Check all DSP modes that apply',1240,519,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1697,1,'Since this device uses 1 button to toggle DSP Modes, we need to know what order they are in so we can cycle through them. Please confirm the order and click next',1241,519,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1698,1,'DSP Modes Order',1242,519,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1699,1,'Since this device uses 1 button to toggle inputs, we need to know what order those inputs are in so we can cycle through them. Please confirm the order and click next.',1243,519,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1700,1,'Inputs Order',1244,519,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1701,1,'Learn Infrared Code',1245,527,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1702,1,'No, and ignore it every time.  Don\'t ask again for this device.',1246,531,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1703,1,'Toggles Power',1247,535,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1704,1,'You didn\'t install the bonus CD, so you won\'t see or hear any video clips.  Just choose \'Next\' when you can see this screen.',1248,540,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1705,1,'I didn\'t detect a remote control.  Plug-in one a compatible USB remote, or a supported i/r receivers and use a compatible infrared remote control.  The compatible infrared receivers are listed on the screen.\r\n\r\nCompatible infrared receivers: <%=12%>\r\n',1249,931,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1706,1,'There are 2 setup wizards.  ',1250,540,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1707,1,'With this wizard you can configure options for the media playback at this location, including what TV service you have, what model stereo receiver and tv you have, and sound and video options.  Run this wizard on every new media director in the home.',1251,931,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1708,1,'With this wizard you choose options for the whole house, such as the names of your family members, where your home is located and how many rooms it has, what kind of automation, security and phone system you have.',1252,931,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1709,1,'Media Player',1253,782,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1710,1,'House Setup',1254,782,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1711,1,'NOTE: Advanced users can set everything up with more options using the LinuxMCE Admin Web Page.  From any web browser on the same LAN go to: http://<%=LANIP%> or select this option.  It\'s easiest to do the wizard first, though.',1255,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1712,1,'Go To Admin Site',1256,545,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1713,1,'No, I won\'t use a remote',1257,546,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1714,1,'Type a name and select \'Add User\', or select a name and then \'Remove User\'.',1258,546,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1715,1,'Continue without one',1259,549,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1716,1,'First you must include all ZWave devices the in your ZWave master controller.  When you are done, select \'Next\'.',1260,549,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1717,1,'You already have <%=12%> lights in the system.  Is correct?',1261,551,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1718,1,'No, add my lights again',1262,551,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1720,1,'This is connected to a tv: <%=45%> on input <%=43%>.  Is that correct?',1264,551,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1721,1,'This is connected to a tv: <%=45%>.\r\nIs that correct?',1265,551,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1722,1,'No, that is not the TV',1266,551,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1723,1,'That is the TV, but the input is wrong',1267,551,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1724,1,'I didn\'t detect an alarm panel.  If you have one of the compatible plug-and-play alarm panels, plug in the controller now.  I will automatically detect it and set it up for you.  If you have a non-plug and play alarm panel you will need to set it up manually using the LinuxMCE Admin Web Page.\r\n\r\nPlug and play alarm panels: <%=12%>\r\n',1268,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1725,1,'There are 2 ways I can control your TV:  1) Infrared, just like the manufacturers remote control.  This works on nearly all TV\'s, but like any universal remote control it isn\'t 100% reliable.  2) Direct connection via the port on the TV marked \'USB, Serial, RS232, Service, Ethernet\'.  This gives you much more functionality, but not all TV\'s have this feature.\r\n\r\nI didn\'t detect a Direct connect TV.  If you have one of the compatible plug-and-play TV\'s from a manufacturer below, connect it to one of my ports now.  \r\n\r\nPlug and play Direct Connect TV\'s: <%=12%>',1269,891,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1726,1,'Use Infrared',1270,551,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1727,1,'Show direct connect models',1271,551,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1728,1,'You will need to use the LinuxMCE Admin Web Page to set this up then.',1272,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1729,1,'The most common way I can control new a/v equipment is by sending infrared codes to the device just like the manufacturer\'s remote control does.  I can help you setup such a device with this video wizard.  It\'s fast and easy.  If your a/v equipment supports a direct connection, such as USB, RS232 or Ethernet, then I will be able to control the device even better using that direct connection.  However setting up such advanced control is beyond the scope of this video wizard.  To do that you will need to use the LinuxMCE Admin Web Page.\r\n\r\nIf you want to proceed and have me control this device with infrared then I will need to know what infrared codes, or signals, to send the device.  First I will try to find some infrared codes I already have which may work with this device.  If I do not have any infrared codes that work, then I will need you to get the remote control for this device and I will have you press buttons on it and I will learn the codes.\r\n\r\nShall we proceed to setup this device for infrared control? ',1273,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1730,1,'Good news!  I have <%=43%> sets of infrared codes for other models from this manufacturer which may work for your model also. And they include discrete on and off codes, not just toggle power codes.\r\n\r\nDefinition: Toggle power is where there is just one power button, or code, that simply toggles the power on and off.  This makes it very difficult to automate because I may send the \'toggle power\' code to turn the device on, when in fact somebody already turned it on by hand, and I really turned it off.  I can\'t just \'look\' at the device like a human can to see if it\'s already on or off.  Discrete on and off means there are separate codes for on and off.  So I don\'t have to worry about what state the device is in.  Often times manufacturers will have a toggle power button on the remote control for humans, and also have discrete codes for automation systems like me.\r\n\r\nOn the next screen I\'m going to show you buttons for <%=43%> sets of infrared codes  to send the \'on\' and the \'off\' commands.  Go through all <%=43%> sets of on/off commands and see which ones control your device.  Be sure to test each \'on\' command a few times in a row to be sure it not only turns the device on, but that it doesn\'t turn it off again.  If sending the \'on\' command when the tv is already on turns the tv off, then it means your model doesn\'t understand the discrete code.  Select the box \'it toggles\'.  If it works, select \'it works\'.  If it doesn\'t work at all, select \'it doesn\'t work\'.  Are you ready?\r\n',1274,553,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1731,1,'Did you connect my video output directly to the TV?  Or did you connect my video output first to a receiver, and then you connected the receiver\'s video output to the TV?',1275,551,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1732,1,'I have <%=43%> sets of infrared codes for other models from this manufacturer, and they may control your model also.  Unfortunately the only codes I could find are what we call \'toggle\'.  They don\'t work nearly as well as \'discrete\' codes.\r\n\r\nDefinition: Toggle power is where there is just one power button, or code, that simply toggles the power on and off.  This makes it very difficult to automate because I may send the \'toggle power\' code to turn the device on, when in fact somebody already turned it on by hand, and I really turned it off.  I can\'t just \'look\' at the device like a human can to see if it\'s already on or off.  Discrete on and off means there separate codes for on and off.  So I don\'t have to worry about what state the device is in.  Often times manufacturers will have a toggle power button on the remote control for human operators, and also have discrete codes for automation systems like me.\r\n\r\nYou may ask your dealer if he is able to get discrete codes for you.  If so, choose the button \'I have discrete codes\'.  Otherwise please go down the list of <%=43%> codes on the next page and see which one of the \'power\' buttons work your device. If a code works check the box \'this works\', if it does not, check the box \'doesn\'t work\'.  Are you ready?\r\n',1276,553,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1733,1,'My manufacturer still isn\'t on the list',1277,553,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1734,1,'Here\'s a more extensive list',1278,553,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1735,1,'Cancel Wizard',1279,553,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1736,1,'I need to reload the router and perhaps regenerate the user interface, depending on the changes you made.  This may take several minutes.',1280,553,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1737,1,'This screen is reserved for future use.  Please choose next.',1281,554,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1738,1,'Video Res & Audio Setup',1282,573,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1739,1,'Current Room',1283,788,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1740,1,'Is this system in the room <%=12%>',1284,559,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1741,1,'I didn\'t detect a Direct connect Receiver.  If you have one, plug it in now.  Or I can control one with infrared.\r\n\r\nPlug and play Direct Connect Receivers: <%=12%>',1285,564,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1742,1,'This is connected to a receiver: <%=45%> on input <%=43%>.  Is that correct?',1286,564,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1743,1,'This is connected to a receiver: <%=45%>.\r\nIs that correct?',1287,564,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1744,1,'No, that is not the receiver',1288,564,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1745,1,'That is the receiver, but the input is wrong',1289,564,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1746,1,'Don\'t control my receiver',1290,564,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1747,1,'A video clip should play here if you have installed the bonus cd',1291,565,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1748,1,'Public',1292,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1749,1,'All',1293,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1750,1,'Go',1294,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1751,1,'Format',1295,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1752,1,'Type',1296,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1753,1,'Genre',1297,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1754,1,'Rating',1298,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1755,1,'Private',1299,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1756,1,'Source',1300,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1757,1,'What?',1301,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1758,1,'Sort',1302,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1759,1,'File: <%=KFILE%>',1303,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1760,1,'<%=KTITLE%>',1304,567,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1761,1,'Video',1305,568,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1762,1,'Pictures',1306,568,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1763,1,'Games',1307,568,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1764,1,'Data',1308,568,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1765,1,'Audio',1309,569,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1766,1,'You connected a <%=DEVICE%>.  <%=ROOM%>\r\nShall I use it?',1310,591,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1767,1,'I think it is in the room <%=ROOM%>',1311,591,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1768,1,'Yes, but that is not the room',1312,591,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1769,1,'Select your city from the list below, or, if it\'s not shown, try searching for another larger city',1313,591,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1770,1,'Error retrieving longitude, latitude and time zone for that city.  Please try another city, perhaps a nearby larger one',1314,591,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1771,1,'No more A/V devices',1315,591,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1772,1,'Add Software',1316,591,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1773,1,'Waiting for the new device to startup....  One moment, please.',1317,592,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1774,1,'The device failed to start properly.  Something is not right.',1318,592,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1775,1,'Which lights are in proximity to this camera and should be turned on when it\'s active?',1319,597,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1776,1,'I found your security system, <%=12%>, but it doesn\'t seem to be controlling any sensors.  Please confirm that it has sensors attached, and add them manually using the LinuxMCE Admin Web Page.',1320,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1777,1,'Confirm Sensors',1321,601,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1778,1,'There are a total of <%=12%> sensors in the house.\r\nThere are <%=13%> sensors that have not yet been assigned to a room which we must identify.  Select Next to start.',1322,601,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1779,1,'Your security panel <%=12%> is already setup.  If you want to make changes please use the LinuxMCE Admin Web Page.',1323,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1780,1,'Which room is this sensor in?\r\n<%=43%>',1324,605,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1781,1,'What shall we call this sensor?\r\n<%=43%>',1325,605,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1782,1,'What type of sensor is this?\r\n<%=43%>',1326,605,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1783,1,'Title: <%=CAH:5137.0.0.5138:Title%>\r\n<%=CAH:5137.0.0.5138:Description%>\r\n',1327,617,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1784,1,'Are you sure you want to add the following software?  If you say yes, your request will be queued, and it may take up to 30 minutes to complete downloading and installation before it shows up as installed.  Please be patient.',1328,769,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1785,1,'Are you sure you want to delete the following software?  If you say yes, your request will be queued, and may take a couple minutes to complete before it shows up on the list as not installed.',1329,769,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1786,1,'Choose Folder',1330,622,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1787,1,'Choose',1331,622,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1788,1,'Create Directory',1332,622,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1789,1,'Choose Drive',1333,623,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1790,1,'In directory: <%=33%>\r\n[change]',1334,624,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1791,1,'Save to: <%=31%>\r\n[change]',1335,624,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1792,1,'Add Device',1336,632,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1793,1,'Your device was added but some configuration data is missing. This data can only be fetched from the Internet. This device won\'t work until you connect to the Internet',1337,639,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1794,1,'Resend A/V codes',1338,639,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1795,1,'View Attributes',1339,639,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1796,1,'Bookmarks',1340,639,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1797,1,'Manage Playlist',1341,639,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1798,1,'Arrows',1342,646,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1799,1,'Set as Start Point',1343,648,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1800,1,'Your password is the same with username at this time. You can change it later using the LinuxMCE Admin Web Page.',1344,1013,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1801,1,'You must create at least 1 room for this system',1345,648,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1802,1,'Filter/Sort',1346,649,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1806,1,'<%=NP_MT%>',1350,655,33129,0,'0000-00-00 00:00:00',NULL),(1807,1,'Your username for the LinuxMCE Admin Web Page and network file 